+// computed by the same arithmetic, in the same order and with the same rounding points as those
+// three kernels; only the thread mapping and the memory traffic change:
+//
+//   blocks [0, H)   b/a GEMV and beta/g for v head h. Warp w computes output (w & 1) * H + h
+//                   for CONV_BA_ROWS rows at once, each row's sum being the original warp's: lane
+//                   l accumulates half2 elements l, l + 32, ... in ascending order with the same
+//                   two fmaf per element, then the same __shfl_down_sync tree, then the bias. The
+//                   loads are hoisted CONV_BA_UNROLL elements ahead (addresses only), and the
+//                   weight row is read once for all rows instead of once per row. beta/g use the
+//                   fused_op_3 formula on the fp32 sums (still stored to ba, bit-identical).
+//   other blocks    causal conv1d update, one thread per (batch row, channel), reading the fp32
+//                   qkv projection directly: trunc_bf16 (the value fused_op_3 stored to
+//                   mixed_qkv) then __bfloat162float (the value conv1d_update read back), so the
+//                   conv sees identical inputs without the [B,F,S] round trip. The window FMA
+//                   chain, activation and rounding are conv1d_update_kernel's. The state window
